@*
    Task 15.1 — the ASP.NET Core replacement for this plugin's web.config
    <system.web.webPages.razor><pages> element (Requirement 4.4).

    THIS FILE IS PART OF THE PLUGIN RECIPE. Every plugin that ships a .cshtml needs one; see
    src/Plugins/Nop.Plugin.DiscountRules.CustomerRoles/Views/_ViewImports.cshtml for the full
    reasoning. In brief: all 20 plugins ship a byte-identical web.config declaring
    pageBaseType="Nop.Web.Framework.ViewEngines.Razor.WebViewPage" (→ the @inherits below, which
    is what makes T("…") resolve and an unqualified @model bind) plus four System.Web <namespaces>
    (→ the @using directives; System.Web.Mvc.Ajax has no ASP.NET Core counterpart and is dropped).

    It must sit at Views/ and inside the project file's Content/Link glob (Views\**\*.cshtml), so
    that this file, Configure.cshtml, _FixedRate.cshtml and _CountryStateZip.cshtml all link into
    the SAME directory (/Plugins/Tax.FixedOrByCountryStateZip/Views/) — Razor resolves imports by
    walking up from the view's LINKED path.

    NOTE Configure.cshtml and _CountryStateZip.cshtml both declare `@model … .ConfigurationModel`
    fully QUALIFIED, and _FixedRate.cshtml has no @model, so the
    @using Nop.Plugin.Tax.FixedOrByCountryStateZip.Models below is not strictly required by them —
    it is present for consistency with the other plugins and so an unqualified @model added later
    resolves.
*@
@inherits Nop.Web.Framework.ViewEngines.Razor.WebViewPage<TModel>

@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Html
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Rendering
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Routing

@*
    Nop.Web.Framework carries HtmlExtensions (Html.NopLabelFor / NopEditorFor /
    NopDropDownListFor / FieldIdFor / ValidationMessageFor bridge), ViewCompatibilityExtensions
    and ChildActionExtensions. Extensions.SelectionIsNotPossible (used by the store dropdown in
    _CountryStateZip.cshtml) is in the same namespace. One import covers all of them.
*@
@using Nop.Core.Infrastructure
@using Nop.Web.Framework
@using Nop.Web.Framework.UI
@using Nop.Plugin.Tax.FixedOrByCountryStateZip.Models

@*
    Tag helpers. 3.90 had none (they do not exist in MVC 5). Added for the same reason task 7.3
    added them to Nop.Web: the framework's form/validation tag helpers are the supported route to
    an anti-forgery token, and Html.BeginForm uses the same infrastructure.
*@
@addTagHelper *, Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers
